      "message": "feat(2d): rest Adaptive planned on proved remaining stock\n\nAdd camcraft_motion::machining2d::rest_adaptive: the 2D rest generator\nfor the Adaptive strategy. It is given, per cut depth, the legal\ncutter-center area and a conservative bound on the material the earlier\noperations left (RestStock: proved floors, each with what remains and\nwhat the proof could not decide), and never assumes anything cut.\n\n- Stock, depth and entry guards: uncertain stock stands as material; a\n  cut depth below every proved floor is refused by name before anything\n  is planned; a plunge needs the whole cutter footprint, with a margin,\n  proved clear by the stock as given (asked of the polygon and of the\n  raster). Each guard has a pinning test that fails with it switched\n  off.\n- The stock raster is conservative: every cell the bound touches\n  stands. A film thinner than RestStock::film() is safety material but\n  gets no pass.\n- Passes are the boundary of the room the cutter may stand in without\n  biting deeper than the step, opened by a disc whose radius falls\n  phase by phase: arcs tangent to the walls in a corner, half loops\n  across a neck, closed rings round a free-standing piece. Every feed\n  is walked on the raster before it is kept; there is no overload\n  fallback.\n- Passes that ride a wall ride it on one fixed vertex list and retrace\n  the area's earlier way in and out, so the verifier's crossing law\n  holds; each candidate is still asked that law.\n- Refused by name: unproved stock, a missing cut depth, no proved\n  entry, a load or coverage that cannot be proved, a plan past its\n  budget, nothing left.\n\nThe Pocket operation's parameter door still refuses Adaptive for rest\nmachining: it only has an entered previous tool, which is no proof.\nDeriving the stock from the earlier operations is issue 2033.\n\nFixes #2031\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
