      "message": "fix(motion): hold rest Adaptive air feed and retracts to a budget\n\nA rest pass is now reached back along the pass just cut (the same\nchords reversed, so no crossing), not by riding the walls in from the\narea's first landing and back on one chord. An area is planned in cells\nat most 4 tool diameters wide, so a neck's two mouths are no longer cut\nalternately with a retract between. Each depth is held to a travel\nbudget of its own - feed out of cut at most 3x the feed in cut, read on\nthe material the passes remove, and at most one retract per rest area\nafter the first plus the plain Adaptive's 8 - refused by name past it.\n\nCorner fixture: air feed 967 -> 562 mm; neck: 37 -> 10 plunges a depth,\nair feed 3445 -> 1979 mm. Every law of tests/rest_adaptive still holds.\n\nFixes #2109\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
